===Verb===
{{en-verb|~s|ghostwriting|ghostwrote|ghostwritten}}

# {{lb|en|authorship|intransitive}} To write under the name of another (especially [[literary]] works).
#: {{ux|en|Mariana would rather not '''ghostwrite''' for a living because she finds it a thankless task.}}
# {{lb|en|authorship|transitive}} To [[author]] a literary work or [[speech]] in the place of another.
#: {{ux|en|The president has someone to '''ghostwrite''' his addresses.}}
#* {{RQ:NYT|date=04-09-2018|author=w:Melanie Thernstrom|title=The Father of Personal Computing Who Was Also a Terrible Dad|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20180905012931/https://www.nytimes.com/2018/09/04/books/review/lisa-brennan-jobs-small-fry.html|passage=Before I read her book, I wondered if it had been '''ghostwritten''', like many such books.}}

